## Closing thoughts

You made it through the whole guide. That is not a small thing — this project touches networking, security scoring, government threat feeds, async Python, databases, message queues, and authenticated APIs.

You don't need to memorize every file. Keep this document nearby. When you see an unfamiliar word, check Section 2. When you wonder "what runs when I click scan," check Section 5. When something breaks, check Section 10.

The code is organized so that each piece has one job. That makes it learnable — one layer at a time.

Welcome to vuln_aggregator. Go break things in a test environment first.
